  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 128 AM CDT Sun Jul 5 2026\n\nThere will be a low chance for showers and thunderstorms across the \nCoastal Plains Sunday and into early next week along the sea breeze. \nAnything that develops is expected to be short lived with low \nrainfall accumulations. As we head into next week, a mid-level ridge \nwill build into the region keeping us warm and maintain our rain \nchances on the lower end. \n\nAbove normal temperature combining with ample low-level moisture \nwill promote heat index values between 100-110 degrees through the \nSunday and into early next week. Please use caution if you're \nworking or playing outside. Take plenty of breaks, drink water, and \ndon't forget sunscreen.\n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat",
